# Wave W17-T (Route 133): rapid rock — rapid channel rock standing in the lane\u2019s water: a dark blue-grey channel rock drawn with longer joints — two long dark joint lines running the rock\u2019s length, the faster water\u2019s stone, worn smooth and drawn out by the flow; foam collar at its base, the sea baked in around it. Route 133\u2019s own rock — the fleet\u2019s only long-jointed lane rock: split from Route 132\u2019s even-jointed stream rock by the drawn joints themselves and from Route 134\u2019s pale spray-wet gate rock by value (dark flow stone vs falls-lit stone).
